WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.909 --> 00:00:08.129
Chris Hardwick is the king of the Nerdist
empire and AMC's many live after-shows.

00:00:08.129 --> 00:00:13.490
He's hosted Talking Dead, Talking Bad, Talking
Saul, Singled Out, and at midnight, among

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:14.490
others.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:15.980
But there's more to him than that.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.910
Let's go beyond the nerdy exterior and take
a look at some of the things you probably

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.490
didn't know about Chris Hardwick.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:23.490
Bowling is in his blood

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.789
He’s a guy who seems to have done just about
everything.

00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:29.760
But one career he hasn't pursued?

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.760
Professional bowling.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:35.610
Sure, most people don't go into bowling as
a real job, but Chris actually had pretty

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.430
good reason to consider it.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.980
His parents met at a bowling alley owned by
his grandfather.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:45.660
Chris' father, Billy Hardwick, was a professional
bowler who won 18 Professional Bowlers Association

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.270
titles, and was elected into the PBA Hall
of Fame in 1977.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:54.969
Instead, Chris opted to strike it rich on
television, and has no time to spare to follow

00:00:54.969 --> 00:00:57.000
in his father’s legacy.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.940
He's a legit philosopher

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.149
Chris Hardwick has built a career around his
ability to talk philosophically on just about

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:05.420
any nerdy topic under the sun.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:09.399
But unlike most media pundits, Hardwick is
an actual philosopher.

00:01:09.399 --> 00:01:10.399
Seriously.

00:01:10.399 --> 00:01:15.360
He received a degree in Philosophy from UCLA,
where he was a member of the Chi Phi Fraternity,

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.090
which has included members like legendary
news anchor Walter Cronkite.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:20.440
Why philosophy?

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.039
Hardwick told the Chicago Tribune, "It's perfect
for comedy.

00:01:23.039 --> 00:01:25.220
It forces you to deconstruct."

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.530
He shared quarters with Wesley Crusher

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:32.080
If there's anyone who carries the nerd flag
as proudly as Chris Hardwick, it's Wil Wheaton.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:35.450
Wheaton is known for playing Wesley Crusher
on Star Trek: The Next Generation.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:40.450
“I know this might finish me as an acting
ensign but, Shut Up Wesley”

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:45.250
With hosting duties on the web series TableTop
and appearing on The Big Bang Theory, Wheaton,

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:49.459
like Hardwick, has made an entire career and
life out of being a nerd.

00:01:49.459 --> 00:01:53.539
Amazingly enough, the two geek icons were
actually roommates in college.

00:01:53.539 --> 00:01:59.650
They also met in an appropriately nerdy way:
In line to see the 1990 horror comedy Arachnophobia.

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:02.259
MTV's Singled Out

00:02:02.259 --> 00:02:06.740
In the early '90s, Chris Hardwick got his
big break when he became a DJ at the influential

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:10.830
KROQ 106.7 in Pasadena, California.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.940
Hardwick's radio popularity brought him to
the attention of MTV, who hired him to co-host

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:18.040
their dating show, Singled Out, alongside
Jenny McCarthy.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:23.114
“Take me to the secret garden where all
the other girls are buried”

00:02:23.114 --> 00:02:24.480
The rest is history!

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.990
Well, sort of…

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:28.410
Alcohol addiction

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:32.840
After his stint as host of MTV's Singled Out
came to an end, Hardwick's life went into

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.000
a tailspin due to alcoholism.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.440
He put on weight and found himself in a personal
and professional rut.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:44.030
Finally, he decided to kick alcohol entirely
and go sober, which he speaks openly about.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:47.300
In his self-help memoir The Nerdist Way, Hardwick
comes clean:

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:52.430
"I knew that I had two choices: I could continue
living the way I was living and die pickled

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:57.100
and unemployed, or make sweeping changes with
the hope of salvaging my life."

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.910
Serial killers, supervillains, and the Terminator

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:04.420
While Hardwick is best known for talking about
TV shows and movies, he sometimes stars in

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.420
them too.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:08.420
Well, depending on your definition of "star."

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:13.140
Among his many acting credits are minor roles
in House of 1000 Corpses, Terminator 3: Rise

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:16.220
of the Machines, and as the voice of Green
Arrow on The Batman.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:21.150
“People are getting sick around here and
it is because of that dirt bag Bruce Wayne.”

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:25.420
He's even butted heads with Handsome Jack
as Vaughn in Tales from the Borderlands.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:30.240
But perhaps his greatest role is Otis from
Back at the Barnyard, a male cow with an inexplicable

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:31.270
udder.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.390
That's not how cows work, you guys.

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:35.790
Engaged to an heiress

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:40.130
Over the years, Hardwick has been linked to
several high profile starlets, including actresses

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.920
Jacinda Barrett and Janet Varney.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:48.010
In 2015, he finally became engaged to one
of the richest women in the world, Lydia Hearst.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:52.130
An actress and fashion model, Lydia is the
daughter of infamously unwilling bank robber

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.250
Patty Hearst.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:57.131
She’s also an heir to the fortune of her
deceased great-grandfather, the legendary

00:03:57.131 --> 00:03:59.660
publishing magnate William Randolph Hearst.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.790
That’s a whole lot of comic books for Chris.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:04.990
He's a serious businessman

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:08.200
Being the world's preeminent nerd isn't just
a full time job.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.820
It's also big business.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:12.370
In 2008, Hardwick founded Nerdist.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:17.140
Three years later, Nerdist merged with GeekChicDaily
to form Nerdist Industries, and later, he

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:19.060
became its Chief Creative Officer.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:23.900
And when Nerdist Industries was purchased
by Legendary Entertainment a year later, Hardwick

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.310
was promoted to co-president of their digital
business.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:30.720
It just proves that you can't be the top geek
without having a serious helping of smarts.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:32.310
Thanks for watching!

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:35.650
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:39.159
And leave us a comment to let us know what
surprised you most about Chris Hardwick...

